00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:16.640
And now, check this out. Here, this AI technique&nbsp;
looked at videos of people in real conversations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:23.920
and then, all we need is our audio input.&nbsp;
Then, get this, it creates virtual characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:31.240
mouth movements and even gestures automatically&nbsp;
so we can have conversations in virtual worlds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:43.960
more easily. I have to say the synthesized&nbsp;
movements are often expressive, I give you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:50.640
that, but also sometimes a little stiff,&nbsp;
mouth movement is not that accurate yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:57.480
but it is very impressive that from just the&nbsp;
audio, all this can be synthesized. Once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:03.280
just two more papers down the line, and you might&nbsp;
start seeing this out there in the real world.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:10.520
I think this work is a really good showcase of how&nbsp;
difficult this problem is. You see, our brains are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:18.160
wired to look at each other, and read each other’s&nbsp;
expressions. Thus, if even a little hesitation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:25.040
just a tiny smirk, if just the slightest things&nbsp;
are off, we immediately know that something is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:32.360
wrong. We are wired for that. So making this&nbsp;
work properly will be incredibly difficult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:38.400
but if something, human ingenuity and&nbsp;
the power of AI will be able to do that.

